 {\centerline{\resizebox{0.71\columnwidth}{!}{\includegraphics{Figures/Fig_network_topology.png}}}}
 \vspace{-0.8em}
 \caption{A schematic of the multiuser RIS-aided network}
 \label{fig:network}
\end{figure}
In our simulations, a three-dimensional Cartesian coordinate system is adopted to define the spatial locations of the network entities.
Fig.~\ref{fig:network} presents a top-down view of the simulation setup projected onto the $xy$-plane.
Specifically, the BS and the RIS are located at $(0, 0, 10)$ m and $(25, 20, 5)$ m, respectively. 
The users are randomly distributed within a circular region of radius 20 m at a height of 1.7 m. 
