Furthermore, we evaluate whether the fixed Gaussian-reference Bussgang moments remain representative after beamforming optimization by collecting the final continuous RIS latent vectors $\breve{\bphi}_r^\star$ before phase quantization.
Their actual quantization residuals are defined as
\begin{align}
\bq_r \triangleq \cQ(\breve{\bphi}_r^\star)
-\beta_{\rm ref}\breve{\bphi}_r^\star,
\end{align}
where $\beta_{\rm ref}$ is fixed before optimization.
The empirical gain is fitted separately as
\begin{align}
 \widehat{\beta} = \frac{\sum_{r=1}^{R}\breve{\bphi}_r^{\star {\sf H}}\cQ(\breve{\bphi}_r^\star)
 }{\sum_{r=1}^{R}\|\breve{\bphi}_r^\star\|^2}.
\end{align}
In addition, we report its real part together with the normalized auto-covariance and cross-covariance metrics
\begin{align}
\delta_{\rm auto}
=
\frac{
\big\|\widehat{\mathbf C}_{\bq\bq}
-\mathbf C_{\bq\bq}^{\rm ref}\big\|_F
}{\big\|\bC_{\bq\bq}^{\rm ref}\big\|_F
},\;\;
\delta_{\rm cross}
=
\frac{
\big\|\widehat{\mathbf C}_{\bq\breve{\bphi}}\big\|_F
}{\sqrt{\big\|\bC_{\bq\bq}^{\rm ref}\big\|_F \big\|\bC_{\breve{\bphi}\breve{\bphi}}^{\rm ref}\big\|_F}},
\end{align}
where $\mathbf C_{\bq\bq}^{\rm ref}\triangleq(1-\beta_{\rm ref}^{2})\mathbf I_M$ and $\mathbf C_{\breve{\bphi}\breve{\bphi}}^{\rm ref}\triangleq\mathbf I_M$, and also $\widehat{\mathbf C}_{\bq\bq}$ and $\widehat{\mathbf C}_{\bq\breve{\bphi}}$ denote the empirical auto- and cross-covariance matrices.
Table~\ref{tab:fixed_bussgang_moments} compares post-optimization moments with analytical and reference benchmarks.
Each Gaussian benchmark is the median of the corresponding empirical metric over independently generated ensembles with $M=50$ and $R=10^4$ as the optimized ensemble.
For both phase resolutions, the empirical gain closely matches its analytical value, and the normalized cross-covariance and auto-covariance error magnitude are comparable to the Gaussian benchmarks.
These results provide empirical support for using fixed Gaussian-reference moments in the proposed distortion-aware surrogates.
