\begin{verbatim}
ALGORITHM: Segment-then-Map Anatomical Extraction
INPUT: Cleaned CT findings (text), Target Organ List
OUTPUT: Structured JSON Map (Organ: Finding)
INSTRUCTION SET:
1.  LOCALIZE_CONTEXT:
 - Identify sentences specific to each Target Organ.
 - Validate finding ownership (e.g., exclude "peri-pancreatic" from Pancreas).
2.  LATERALIZATION_RESOLVER:
 - Map plural descriptors (e.g., "Kidneys") to both lateral child nodes.
 - Isolate unilateral findings strictly to the specific side (Right/Left).
3.  EVIDENCE_HIERARCHY_DECISION:
 - IF PATHOLOGY_DETECTED:
 - Identify: Calcification, cyst, nodule, stone, surgical change.
 - ACTION: Extract verbatim clinical snippet.
 - ELSE IF EXPLICIT_NORMAL:
 - Identify: "normal", "unremarkable", "no findings".
 - ACTION: Inject EXACT string from Standardized Template Pool.
 - ELSE:
 - ACTION: Assign "Unremarkable" (Indicates omission/absence).
4.  PATHOLOGY_GUARDRAIL:
 - Explicitly inhibit Template Injection if any secondary findings 
 (e.g., fat infiltration, resections, clips) are identified.
EXECUTION:
- Iterate through Target Organ List.
- Perform high-fidelity mapping of sub-segments (e.g., Rectum -> Colon).
- Output strictly validated JSON schema.
\end{verbatim}
