\section{Datasets}
\label{sec:appendixdatasets}
\begin{figure}[t]
 \centering
 \includegraphics[width=\linewidth]{Figures/ct_phases.png}
 \caption{\textbf{Multi-phase contrast-enhanced CT scans.} In our pre-training and evaluation, we utilize multi-phase CT volumes encompassing non-contrast, arterial (25--35~s), portal-venous (60--70~s), and delayed ($>$3 min) phases. We demonstrate the diversity of hemodynamic enhancement patterns across these temporal windows; as illustrated, each phase provides unique voxel intensities for the same anatomical structures. This multi-temporal alignment enables the model to learn robust anatomy-normality representations and capture temporal-spectral dependencies that are typically absent in single-phase medical vision-language datasets.}
 \label{fig:phasesoverview}
\end{figure}
In this section, we provide a detailed description of the datasets used in the pre-training, testing, and fine-tuning stages.
\subsection{Training}
To train our model, we curate a large-scale, multimodal, multi-center dataset comprising both public and proprietary sources. This collection includes 67,331 multi-phase CT scans across 53,643 exams from 37,989 patients, each paired with its corresponding radiology report. Detailed descriptions of the individual cohorts are provided below, and Table \ref{tab:appendix_training_datasets} summarizes the dataset distributions.
