\section{Notation}
Throughout the paper, we denote the batch size by~$B$ and the number of
segmentation classes, including background, by~$C$ ($C=15$ in pre-training), with $d_e$ denoting the dimension
of the shared vision--text embedding space.  An input volume
$\mathbf{X}\in\mathbb{R}^{B\times 1\times D\times H\times W}$ is paired with a
voxel-wise label map $L\in\{0,\dots,C{-}1\}^{B\times D\times H\times W}$, and
the pyramid encoder produces MoE-refined features
$\mathbf{X}_s\in\mathbb{R}^{B\times C_s\times D_s\times H_s\times W_s}$ at four
stages $s\in\{1,\dots,4\}$, with $K_s$ experts per stage. Let $N_s$ denote the number of projector key/value tokens after any strided convolution.
At stage~$s$ the A$^{2}$MoE router combines a global context $\mathbf{v}_s$, a
crop-level routing representation $\widetilde{\mathbf h}=\mathcal T(\mathbf h)$, where each raw histogram $\mathbf h\in\Delta^{C-1}$ is replaced at inference
by the stage-specific composition estimate $\hat{\mathbf h}_s$ before normalization, and a log-prior built from a
learnable affinity matrix $\mathbf{A}^{(s)}\!\in\!\mathbb{R}^{C\times K_s}$,
producing expert weights $\mathbf W_s$ from the joint route $\Psi_{\rm gate}^{(s)}$, direct route $\Psi_{\rm anat}^{(s)}$, and structural prior; the stage-specific coefficient
$\beta_s>0$ controls the prior's strength and $\epsilon$ stabilizes its
logarithm.  On top of the encoder, the OQMSP uses a single set of
organ queries $\mathbf{Q}\!\in\!\mathbb{R}^{(C-1)\times d_e}$ shared across
stages, produces per-stage, per-organ embeddings $\hat{\mathbf{E}}_s$, and
fuses them with softmax-normalized weights $\boldsymbol{\alpha}$ into
$\mathbf{Z}_{\text{vis}}\!\in\!\mathbb{R}^{B\times(C-1)\times d_e}$, which is
aligned via a learnable log-temperature $\log\tau$ with text embeddings
$\mathbf{z}_{\text{txt}}\!\in\!\mathbb{S}^{d_e-1}$ drawn from a frozen
PubMedBERT through a projection head $\phi_{\text{txt}}$. The final objective weights are segmentation, anatomy-conditioned routing, organ--text alignment, cross-stage consistency, and query-grounding losses 
$\lambda_{\rm seg},\lambda_{\rm MoE},\lambda_{\rm align},\lambda_{\rm stage},\lambda_{\rm ground}$.
