\section{Conclusion}\label{sec:con}
In this paper, we considered the worst-user outage probability minimization problem in active RIS-aided systems. By combining a probability-simplex user weighting reformulation, a softplus surrogate, and entropic tail-risk aggregation, we developed the data-driven stochastic optimization technique.
Simulation results demonstrate that the proposed technique can be an effective solution for reliability-oriented active RIS transmission design.
