\section{Simulation Results}
This section presents numerical results to assess the effectiveness of the proposed algorithms for the MA-assisted covert communication system. Unless otherwise specified, $M=6$, $K_o=K_c=Q=2$, $P=0$ dBW, and the noise power at all users and wardens is $-80$ dBW. Alice is located at the origin of a $60$ m $\times$ $60$ m field, and all users and wardens have a single fixed antenna. Overt users 1 and 2 are randomly placed in disks of radius $r_o=15$ m centered $60$ m from Alice at $70^\circ$ and $110^\circ$, respectively. Each disk contains one covert user and one warden. The linear transmit region has length $A=12\lambda$, with $\lambda=0.1$ m and minimum MA spacing $x_{th}=\lambda/2$. Each user channel contains one LoS path and $L_k-1$ non-line-of-sight (NLoS) paths, with $L_k=3$. The independent path gains satisfy $\beta_k^1\sim\mathcal{CN}\bigl(0,{\kappa c_k^2}/(\kappa+1)\bigr)$ for the LoS path and $\beta_k^\ell\sim\mathcal{CN}\bigl(0,{c_k^2}/{((\kappa+1)(L_k-1))}\bigr)$ for the NLoS paths, where $\ell=2,\ldots,L_k$ and $\kappa=2$. The large-scale path loss is $c_k^2=C_0d_k^{-\alpha_{\mathrm{PL}}}$, where $d_k$ is the link distance in meters, $C_0=-30$ dB, and $\alpha_{\mathrm{PL}}=2.6$. Similarly, the warden channel gain is $\beta_q=c_qe^{\jmath\phi_q}$, where $\phi_q\sim\mathcal{U}[0,2\pi)$, $c_q^2=C_0d_q^{-\alpha_{\mathrm{PL}}}$, and $d_q$ is the link distance in meters. The LoS azimuth angles are determined by the user and warden locations, while the NLoS azimuth angles are independently and uniformly distributed over $[0,\pi]$. The transmission blocklength is $N=32$, the covertness level is $\epsilon=0.1$, and the covert user priority parameter is $\nu=0.5$.
For a fair comparison between the worst-case and statistical optimization schemes, the CSI uncertainty coefficient is set to $\kappa_{\mathrm{CSI}}=0.01$ and the maximum covertness outage probability is $\varrho_q=0.05$ for every warden. Following the relative error model in~\cite{ZhangRobustCovertISAC}, the statistical error covariance matrix is set to $\boldsymbol E_q=\kappa_{\mathrm{CSI}}\|\bar{\boldsymbol h}_q(\boldsymbol x)\|_2^2\boldsymbol I_M/M$. Accordingly, the bounded-error radius is chosen as $e_q^2=\frac{\kappa_{\mathrm{CSI}}\|\bar{\boldsymbol h}_q(\boldsymbol x)\|_2^2}{2M}F_{\chi_{2M}^2}^{-1}(1-\varrho_q)$, where $F_{\chi_{2M}^2}^{-1}$ denotes the inverse cumulative distribution function of a chi-square distribution with $2M$ DoFs. 
