\section{Conclusion}\label{sec:conclusion}
In this paper, we investigated a robust MA-assisted covert communication system with multiple wardens under imperfect CSI.
A weighted max-min SINR maximization problem was formulated by jointly optimizing the transmit beamforming vectors, AN covariance matrix, and MA positions.
Both norm-bounded and statistical warden CSI errors were considered.
Specifically, for norm-bounded CSI errors, we developed a BCD-based algorithm incorporating the S-procedure, SDR, and SCA methods.
For statistical CSI errors, we first derived a tractable deterministic approximation of the covertness outage constraints using the Bernstein-type inequality.
Building upon the proposed BCD optimization framework, we developed an outage-constrained optimization scheme.
Simulation results showed that our proposed method can outperform the FPA schemes in terms of weighted max-min SINR.
